# Code owners for the high-risk areas (external audit 35-08).
#
# GitHub requests a review from these owners on any PR that touches a listed
# path. The main ruleset does NOT require code-owner approval today: this is a
# single-maintainer repository and every PR is authored with the owner's own
# account, which GitHub does not let approve its own PR, and the ruleset has no
# bypass actors — requiring it would block every merge. Turn on
# "require_code_owner_review" once a second reviewer exists.
#
# Later patterns win, so the catch-all comes first.

*                                   @ydngemini

